textContent returns every text node including hidden elements and preserves whitespace, while innerText reflects what is visually rendered. Automation scrapers almost always want the trimmed textContent.

code:
const node = document.getElementById('total');
const raw = node.textContent.trim();

real example:
Cypress text assertions use .invoke('text') which reads textContent, so comparing against innerText expectations produces mismatches.
